[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to HTTP Header Injection, specifically CRLF Injection. This vulnerability occurs because the `infoContent` is directly read from user requests and subsequently stored in HTTP response headers without proper sanitization or validation. An attacker could inject malicious newline characters (CRLF, i.e., `%0d%0a`) into the `infoContent`, allowing them to add arbitrary HTTP headers, manipulate existing ones, or even inject response body content. This direct incorporation of unsanitized user input into HTTP headers bypasses security controls and can lead to various attacks, including cache poisoning, cross-site scripting (XSS) if the injected headers are reflected, or session fixation.

